This script logs keystrokes in a normal Windows environment. You can replace the `A B C D E` loop with any keystrokes you want to log. Simply copy and paste the script into a text editor and save it. Then, run the script and it will log every keystroke you type in the program.

Note: This script is more of a demonstration of how to log keystrokes in a Windows environment. It's not designed for production use or a large-scale log collection. Always ensure that you have the necessary permissions and access rights to log keystrokes in a production environment.
